cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this research code or its reported results, please cite this
  repository and the upstream model, datasets and methods described in the README.
type: software
title: "Truthfulness LoRA: Evaluating SFT, F2-Lite and DPO on Qwen3-1.7B"
authors:
  - family-names: Lim
    given-names: Gechleng
    affiliation: Wentworth Institute of Technology
repository-code: "https://github.com/Crient/truthfulness-lora"
url: "https://github.com/Crient/truthfulness-lora"
abstract: >-
  An educational, exploratory comparison of the released Qwen3-1.7B checkpoint,
  HaluEval supervised LoRA, F2-Lite and SFT-initialized UltraFeedback DPO on
  817 frozen TruthfulQA questions. Reported MC1 and MC2 results use a matched
  native-chat likelihood protocol and do not establish generated-answer factual
  accuracy, cross-seed robustness or a DPO-specific causal effect.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - parameter-efficient fine-tuning
  - LoRA
  - direct preference optimization
  - TruthfulQA
